---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-26-record-import.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-26',
  title: 'New workflow page: Import Records With Scout',
  tags: ['workflows', 'scout', 'import', 'seo'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 26, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added a workflow page at
    <a href="/workflows/record-import" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/record-import</a>
    describing how Scout brings existing records into BreederHQ.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">New file</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><code>src/pages/workflows/record-import.astro</code>: three separate imports, each in its own section: general records (animals and contacts, ownership decisions, duplicate handling, registration-number review), litter records, and finance history. States that pedigree ancestors become recorded ancestors and join the breeder's own animals only when explicitly added, and that nothing is saved before review. Includes FAQPage and HowTo structured data.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">SEO</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The new page is picked up by the generated sitemap on the next build. No screenshots yet; they follow separately. Navigation, the workflows index, and feature listings are wired in a separate change.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
